imx6sx-blaze: RMII clocking for ENET1

board_init() calls setup_fec(), which sets ENET1 up for the SABRE-SD's RGMII
PHY: GPR1[13] cleared and a 125 MHz anatop clock. ENET1 here is RMII with the
50 MHz reference on the pad, so select that and run the anatop clock at 50 MHz.
ENET2 is left as it was.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific]
---
--- a/board/freescale/mx6sxsabresd/mx6sxsabresd.c
+++ b/board/freescale/mx6sxsabresd/mx6sxsabresd.c
@@ -167,13 +167,14 @@
 	struct anatop_regs *anatop = (struct anatop_regs *)ANATOP_BASE_ADDR;
 	int reg, ret;
 
-	/* Use 125M anatop loopback REF_CLK1 for ENET1, clear gpr1[13], gpr1[17]*/
-	clrsetbits_le32(&iomuxc_regs->gpr[1], IOMUX_GPR1_FEC1_MASK, 0);
+	/* ENET1 is RMII: take the 50 MHz reference from the pad, gpr1[13] set. */
+	clrsetbits_le32(&iomuxc_regs->gpr[1], IOMUX_GPR1_FEC1_MASK,
+			IOMUX_GPR1_FEC1_CLOCK_MUX2_SEL_MASK);
 
 	/* Use 125M anatop loopback REF_CLK1 for ENET2, clear gpr1[14], gpr1[18]*/
 	clrsetbits_le32(&iomuxc_regs->gpr[1], IOMUX_GPR1_FEC2_MASK, 0);
 
-	ret = enable_fec_anatop_clock(0, ENET_125MHZ);
+	ret = enable_fec_anatop_clock(0, ENET_50MHZ);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
